  factText: Mycelium can grow into bricks and panels. By mixing fungal spores with
    agricultural waste (like straw or sawdust) in molds, you get solid building blocks.
    Once dried, these mycelium bricks are surprisingly strong and fireproof, and
    they biodegrade safely after use.
